/target

# A locally built libverovio.so, where `just verovio-build` puts it by
# default. Verovio is never vendored into this repository and never
# committed — it is a separate, replaceable file, which is what ADR-0007's
# licence reasoning rests on. See THIRD_PARTY.md.
/.verovio-build

# `docs/` is an independent git repository (remote: hogwash-docs).
# It is deliberately not tracked here — see the plan and 004 §15.
/docs

# The frontend's dependencies and build output. `package-lock.json` IS
# committed — it is the only record of exactly which JavaScript went into a
# build, and the Rust half has `Cargo.lock` for the same reason.
/app/node_modules
/app/dist

# Tauri regenerates these JSON schemas from the plugin set on every build.
# They are derived, not authored; `capabilities/` beside them is authored and
# IS committed, because it is where the application's permissions are stated.
/app/src-tauri/gen/schemas
/app/src-tauri/target

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local design reference screenshots, not part of the project.
/ideal-pics
/picofcurrentapp
